# Accepted risks for Trivy (read automatically from the repository root by trivy-action).
# They concern the Terraform code in infra/.
# Every entry needs a reason. Review this list when the architecture changes.

# The backend ALB is internet-facing, but its security group only accepts CloudFront's
# IP ranges (AWS-managed prefix list) and the listener only forwards requests that carry
# the secret X-Origin-Verify header. Improvement: CloudFront VPC origins + internal ALB.
AWS-0053

# CloudFront -> ALB uses HTTP because the project has no custom domain/ACM certificate.
# Viewer -> CloudFront is HTTPS. Improvement: custom domain + ACM certificate on the ALB.
AWS-0054

# The Terraform state bucket uses SSE-S3 (AES256) instead of a customer-managed KMS key.
# Acceptable for a lab; a company would use SSE-KMS with its own key.
AWS-0132
